"""
OHT ANIMATION AUTOMATED (FOR TESTING ONLY):
OHT Fleet Controller  —  automatic track, multiple OHTs, no collisions
=====================================================================
Run in Omniverse / Isaac Sim:  Window > Script Editor > paste > Run (Ctrl+Enter).
Re-running the script rebuilds the fleet cleanly.
To stop it:  run   import builtins; builtins._oht_fleet.stop()

NEW ENVIRONMENT (completely different file / layout) — QUICK START
  1. Bring into the new stage: the rail CAD, one OHT model, one ground machine
     and one magazine (from an old file: right-click > Export Selected, then
     drag the .usd into the new stage).
  2. Put the OHT model ON THE RAIL, in the lane where the fleet should drive,
     facing the driving direction. Put the ground machine under a rail the way
     every machine should stand (its orientation is copied to all new machines).
  3. Set TEMPLATE_PATH, GROUND_MACHINE_TEMPLATE, MAGAZINE_TEMPLATE below to the
     paths of those prims (and RAIL_ROOT to the rail CAD prim if the console
     says it could not find it).
  4. Run. The script then
       * reads the rail CAD and extracts the centre line of every track,
       * builds the track network (junctions, branches),
       * picks a closed loop through the lane the OHT stands on, using only
         moves a real OHT can make at a junction,
       * places ground machines along the loop and magazines on half of them,
       * clones the OHT and drives the fleet: pick up / drop off / queue.
     The extracted track is saved in the stage (/World/OHT_Auto_Track), so the
     next run is instant. Set REBUILD_TRACK = True after changing the rails.

What it does while running
  * Each OHT measures the gap to the vehicle ahead along the rail and cruises,
    slows down smoothly, or stops behind it (never overlaps). Slower in curves.
  * Empty OHTs go to a machine with a magazine: stop, lower the hoist, close
    the claws, lift, carry it to an empty machine, lower, open, raise, leave.

IMPORTANT: if another script/extension is still moving the OHT model, stop it first.
"""

